WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.300
[President Franklin D. Roosevelt dedicates
the National Institute of Health]

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.790
Robert Trout: The President of the United
States dedicates the National Institute of

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:10.790
Health in Bethesda, Maryland.

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:13.740
Six hours ago, the Presidential special train
rolled into Washington's Union Station, bringing

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.830
the President back from his one-day New England
tour, which ended in Boston last night.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:18.830
[Bethesda, Maryland, October 31, 1940]

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:22.420
And now the President has come by automobile
to the National Health Institute in Bethesda,

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.530
Maryland, on the outskirts of Washington.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:29.029
Here on a pleasant Indian summer afternoon,
a moderate sized audience has gathered before

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.740
the white column, red brick administration
building set in the green, rolling Maryland

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:35.870
hills, and surrounded by trees thick with
red and yellow autumn leaves.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.420
[Speaking: Robert Trout, CBS News]

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.730
Announcer: Ladies and gentlemen, the President
of the United States.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.710
[Applause]

00:00:45.710 --> 00:01:02.570
President Roosevelt: Mr. Coy, Dr. Thompson,
the Governor of Maryland, Governor O'Connor,

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.000
ladies and gentlemen.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.240
Nowhere in the world, except in the Americas
is it possible for any nation to devotee great

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:19.380
sector of its effort to life conservation
rather than life destruction.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:25.020
All of us are grateful that we in the United
States can still turn our thoughts and our

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:30.509
attention to those institutions of our country
that symbolize peace.

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:37.359
Institutions whose purpose it is to save life,
and not to destroy it.

00:01:37.359 --> 00:01:44.740
It is for the dedication of these noble buildings
to the service of man that we are assembled

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.840
here today.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:53.840
The National Institute of Health speaks the
universal language of humanitarianism.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:02:04.409
It has been devoted throughout its long, distinguished
history, to furthering the health of all mankind,

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:12.971
in which service, it has recognized no limitations
imposed by international boundaries, and has

00:02:12.971 --> 00:02:19.230
recognized no distinctions of race or creed
or of color.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:27.400
The total defense that we have heard so much
about of late, that total defense which this

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:35.680
nation seeks, involves a great deal more than
building airplanes and ships and guns and

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:36.909
bombs.

00:02:36.909 --> 00:02:42.129
For we cannot be a strong nation unless we
are a healthy nation.

00:02:42.129 --> 00:02:51.000
So we must recruit not only men and materials,
but also knowledge and science to service

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:56.750
our national strength, and that is what we
are doing here.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:03.740
We have recognized the strategic importance
of health by the creation of a Health and

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:10.010
Medical Committee in the Council of National
Defense itself.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:16.599
That committee has the job of coordinating
the health and medical aspects of national

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:18.590
preparedness.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:23.519
That Committee is assisting the government
in the mobilization of the medical and health

00:03:23.519 --> 00:03:30.819
resources of the country to serve the best
interests both of the military and the civilian

00:03:30.819 --> 00:03:33.400
elements of the nation.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:41.659
To do this will require the best energies
of professional and technical leadership everywhere

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:43.060
in the United States.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:49.870
To do this will require the fullest cooperation
between the government and the hospitals,

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:54.219
the medical, the dental, the nursing, and
other professions.

00:03:54.219 --> 00:04:02.670
We seek the same partnership that we seek
for industrial production in the Advisory

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:03.670
Committee.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:14.269
Neither the American people nor their government
intend to socialize medical practice any more

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:19.230
than they plan to socialize industry.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:28.760
In American life, the family doctor, the general
practitioner performs a service which we rely

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.680
upon and which we trust as a nation.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:40.530
No one has a greater appreciation than I of
the skill and self-sacrifice of the medical

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.150
profession.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:49.190
And there can be no substitute for the personal
relationship between doctor and patient, which

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:57.180
is a characteristic and a source of strength
of medical practice in our land.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:05.730
Although we have a great deal to do, the nation
today, I'm very certain, is better prepared

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:12.260
to meet the public health programs of our
emergency than at any previous time in the

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.830
history of the country.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:24.060
Since the passage of the famous Social Security
Act, with its health provisions, in 1935,

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:36.020
federal, state, and local health and medicine
are cooperating more broadly than ever before.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:43.400
Our people are better informed on health matters
than ever before.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:52.210
Scientific knowledge of the causes of disease,
and also the conditions for health has exceeded

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:54.600
any previous limits.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:06:03.340
Facilities for health and medical service
are more numerous and they're better.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:09.680
The Public Health Service of the United States
is a very old institution and it's done magnificent

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:17.770
work, but it has only recently, in the past
few years that the federal government has

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.800
indicated that it can do infinitely more...

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:29.080
that disease disregards state lines as well
as national lines.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:40.560
That among these states there is, as we know,
an inequality of opportunity for health.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:49.020
In such cases, the Public Health Service is
helping and must continue, even more greatly,

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:50.660
to help.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:57.740
That partnership, and I emphasize that word,
in regard to health and medicine throughout

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:06.640
the land, that partnership is making definite
progress among many diseases.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:12.650
Among the buildings of the National Institute
of Health to be dedicated here today, stands

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:20.160
the National Cancer Institute, created through
provisions of the act which I signed on August

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.270
5, 1937.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:27.220
The work of this new institute swell underway.

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:33.660
It is promoting and stimulating cancer research
throughout the nation.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:39.530
It is bringing to the people of the nation
a message of hope, because many forms of the

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:44.910
disease are not only curable, but even preventable.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:52.270
Beyond this it is doing research here and
in many universities to unravel the mysteries

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:53.590
of cancer.

00:07:53.590 --> 00:08:01.330
I think we can all have faith in the ultimate
results of these great efforts.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:08.910
These buildings that we dedicate represent
new and improved housing for an institution

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:16.590
that has a long and accomplished background
of accomplishment in this task of research.

00:08:16.590 --> 00:08:24.360
The original demonstration of the cause and
method of preventing pellagra, for example,

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:29.220
has been followed by other important contributions.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:37.909
Great work has been done in the control of
tularemia, Rocky Mountain Spotted Fever, typhus

00:08:37.909 --> 00:08:43.930
fever, yellow fever, malaria, and sinacotis
[?].

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:53.350
Now that we are less than a day by plane from
the jungle-type yellow fever of South America,

00:08:53.350 --> 00:09:02.439
less than two days from the sleeping sickness
of equatorial Africa, less than three days

00:09:02.439 --> 00:09:13.240
from cholera and bubonic plague, the ramparts
we watch must be civilian in addition to being

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:17.420
military.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:21.589
[Applause]

00:09:21.589 --> 00:09:33.480
For the very beautiful and very spacious grounds
on which these buildings stand, we are indebted

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:49.300
to Mr. and Mrs. Luke Wilson, who wrote to
me in 1935, asking if a part of their estate

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:57.290
in Bethesda, in Maryland, could be used to
the benefit of the people of this nation.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:06.550
I would tell her now, as she sits beside me,
that in the capacity, the compassion of Mr.

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:14.430
and Mrs. Wilson for suffering, in their hope
for human action to alleviate it, she and

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:23.450
her husband symbolize the aspirations of millions
of Americans for a cause such as this, and

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:26.970
we are very grateful.

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:29.790
[Applause]

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:39.959
Today, the need for the conservation of health
and physical fitness is greater than at any

00:10:39.959 --> 00:10:42.589
time in this nation's history.

00:10:42.589 --> 00:10:51.779
In dedicating this institute, I dedicate it
to the underlying philosophy of public health,

00:10:51.779 --> 00:11:02.290
to the conservation of life, to the wise use
of the vital resources of the nation.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:12.259
I voice, for America and for the stricken
world, our hopes, our prayers, our faith in

00:11:12.259 --> 00:11:20.129
the power of man's humanity to man.

00:11:20.129 --> 00:11:25.939
Robert Trout: The President of the United
States has dedicated the National Institute

00:11:25.939 --> 00:11:31.720
of Health, a collection of six buildings set
in the sloping hills of Bethesda, Maryland,

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:37.720
a few miles from Washington.

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:38.920
[Music]

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:49.259
The 
President spoke in this pleasant rural setting

00:11:49.259 --> 00:11:56.110
in Bethesda, Maryland near Washington D.C.
this afternoon after a quick automobile drive

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:01.009
from Washington D.C., the capital city, in
which he arrived a few minutes after ten o'clock

00:12:01.009 --> 00:12:02.029
this morning.

00:12:02.029 --> 00:12:07.970
And now the small audience which has come
out to watch the President dedicate this National

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:11.279
Institute of Health is now moving away and
the President will soon motor back to the

00:12:11.279 --> 00:12:12.640
White House in Washington.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:15.320
This is Bob Trout speaking, this is the Columbia
Broadcasting System.

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:16.320
[President Franklin D. Roosevelt dedicates
the National Institute of Health]

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:17.320
